We must comply by law with UK and EU GDPR, UK DPA (2018), PCI and Sarbanes Oxley (SOX) 
regulations. 
We are audited annually both internally and externally on our compliance with these regulations. 
We have controls in place that are carried out based on control frequency. Daily (i.e. as each 
controlled action occurs), weekly, monthly, quarterly and annually. 
 
we are confident that our controls are comprehensive in all areas. 
Our IT governance framework follows ISO/IEC 27001:13 and NIST standards. 
  
Specific security measures include but are not limited to:  
• Risk management. 
o A comprehensive data, user and cyber security risk management 
process is used by Newsquest to identify and manage risk.  This risk 
management process relates to our own standards, policies, and 
procedures and all our regulatory requirements for GDPR, SOX and PCI.   
• Access control.  
o Access to any system or service is based on the lowest level of access to 
carry out job function. Elevated privileges require additional 
authorisation. Segregation of duty rules apply to all job roles. Access is 
granted only for as long as necessary and a comprehensive management 
process is used to ensure compliance.  
• Physical security. 
o Access to all offices and all sensitive areas have suitable physical access 
controls in place which are reviewed regularly. 
• Data security 
o Data security measures include encryption at rest and in transit. 
Retention and destruction policies are in place. Data integrity 
requirements are defined. 
o Data are protected via network security and specific anti malware, 
filtering and antivirus systems at all levels from perimeter through cloud 
or server infrastructure, at application level and on each end user 
computing device (endpoint).  
• Network security  
o Network segmentation and application layer firewall policies at the 
"perimeter" and internally between segments ensure network access is 
controlled. Only authorised devices and end users have access to 
relevant data and systems. 
o Secure remote access (IPSEC VPN and SSL) systems are used to allow 
authorised personnel secure access to applications.  
o Newsquest has a "Zero trust" approach to all devices connecting to or 
attempting to connect to our systems and services. 
 
 
• Monitoring and incident management. 
o All security systems, network devices, data services, applications and 
servers are monitored. Logging is aggregated into an analysis system to 
enable events to be monitored, identified and incidents responded to 
effectively. 
o Vulnerability scanning and testing is carried out regularly.  
o Newsquest, Gannett and contracted third parties provide 
comprehensive incident management and response. 
• Change control, updates, and patching. 
o All security updates and patches are applied within applicable timescales 
depending on criticality and importance. 
o Change control is a comprehensive process involving suitable review and 
authorisation by appropriate authority.  
• User awareness and involvement. 
o All staff and contractors are made aware of security requirements. 
Information is available to all and regular mandatory training and 
awareness programs ensure staff and contractors are an integral part of 
our security systems